 a typical posture of the subfamily Hesperiinae (Fig. 8). Near the border with Vietnam (Fig. 7: C), it is a very rare species and was discovered at an altitude of 160 meters, not far from villages. In the northern part of its distribution range (Fig. 7: A, B), the adult flies from mid-July to mid-August, while in southern Guangxi (Fig. 7: C) and Hainan it was found in May. The population in Hong Kong is bivoltine with adult on the wing in May and October and diapause as early instar larva in winter. Larvae in Hong Kong (Fig. 9) are known to feed on Indocalamus herklotsii, a bamboo species of Poaceae family.","","text","",""]]},"T9QDL":{"v":[["Cloque de l'érable champêtre","fra",0]],"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","uncertain",""]]},"V5Y8R":{"v":[["Coriander","eng",0],["Koriander","nld",0]]},"VRBD":{"v":[["African Catfish","eng",0],["African Sharptoothed Catfish","eng",0],["Barbel","eng",0],["Catfish","eng",0],["Common Catfish","eng",0],["Mudfish","eng",0],["Sharptooth Catfish","eng",0],["North African catfish","eng",0],["African sharptooth catfish","eng",0],["African walking catfish","eng",0],["Sharptoothed Catfish","eng",0],["Aalbüschelwels","deu",0],["Abu shanab","ara",0],["African mushi","mlf",0],["Afrikanischer Wels","deu",0],["Afrikansk Vandrarmal","swe",0],["Afrikansk ålemalle","dnj",0],["Ambaazaa","orm",0],["Ambaza","amh",0],["Andouma","fan",0],["Arira","ibo",0],["Aro","yor",0],["Balbout","ara",0],["Bambara","wol",0],["Bombe","yao",0],["Bomu","tum",0],["Chibomu","tum",0],["Cá Trê Phi","vie",0],["Garmut","ara",0],["Hotte","ara",0],["Jättikonnamonni","fin",0],["Kambale","swa",0],["Kambale Mumi","swa",0],["Kambali","swa",0],["Karmout Lazeer","ara",0],["Karmut","ara",0],["Kemudu","kau",0],["Kiemensackwels","deu",0],["Klarias","ell",0],["Manguana","loz",0]],"d":[["Kenya","2118","mrgid","",""],["Kenya","2118","mrgid","",""],["Kenya","2118","mrgid","",""],["Kenya","2118","mrgid","",""]]},"ZJFD":{"v":[["Yellow-rumped Seedeater","eng",0],["Yellow-rumped Serin","eng",0],["YRS